# Well known servers, always written first and never dropped by ranking.
#
# ⛔ Two entries, and the second is not a mirror. ArchPOWER publishes from one
# host, and that host sits behind a Cloudflare bot challenge that refuses
# datacentre address ranges. Measured 2026-08-28 from a GitHub runner: every
# request answers 403 with a "Just a moment..." interstitial, for curl's own
# user agent, for pacman's, for a browser's and for this repository's. It is
# the source network, not the identity.
#
# api.rv.pkgforge.dev is a read through proxy in front of the same origin. It
# answered 200 from both a runner and a workstation, with byte identical
# databases: 724493 for powerpc64le, 741715 for powerpc and 684273 for
# powerpc64. HISTORY/powerpc.md carries the measurement.
#
# ⭐ The direct host is first, so a consumer that can reach the origin uses the
# origin and the proxy carries only what cannot. pacman falls through to the
# next Server on a failed transfer, which is what makes the ordering work.
#
# ⚠ The proxy cannot forge a package. SigLevel stays Required and the keyring is
# pinned in bootstrap/keyrings/archpower.pin, so what a proxy could do is serve
# a stale but validly signed set, which is what scripts/check-anchor-floor
# refuses.
Server = https://repo.archlinuxpower.org/$repo/$arch
Server = https://api.rv.pkgforge.dev/https://repo.archlinuxpower.org/$repo/$arch
